# Retrieval Pipeline — Setup & Usage Guide

## What Was Built

A fully structured retrieval pipeline replacing the old POC single-function approach.

```
server/
├── pipeline/          ← The core: triage → respond → format
├── session/           ← JSONL-persisted sessions per user
├── resources/         ← TTL guide cache, static prompt/fallback cache
├── api/server.ts      ← HTTP API (JWT-protected)
├── cli/chat.ts        ← Dev/test interactive CLI
├── core/config.ts     ← All configuration
├── core/schemas.ts    ← All Zod schemas + types
└── prompts/           ← triage.md, respond.md, format.md, format-mdx.md, title.md
```

---

## 1. What to Add to [.env](file:///Users/amritanshu/Desktop/AI%20Chat%20bot/troubleshooting-poc/.env)

Your existing [.env](file:///Users/amritanshu/Desktop/AI%20Chat%20bot/troubleshooting-poc/.env) already has the LLM provider keys. Add these **new entries**:

```env
# ── Sessions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where JSONL session files are stored (created automatically)
SESSIONS_DIR=./data/sessions

# Max user turns per session before quota_exceeded is returned
MAX_TURNS_PER_SESSION=20

# ── Retrieval ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Max clarifying questions per topic window (default 2)
CLARIFICATION_LIMIT=2

# guide.yaml cache TTL in seconds (default 300 = 5 min, 0 = always read from disk)
GUIDE_TTL_SECONDS=300

# ── Format prompt ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "format" = plain markdown (default)
# "format-mdx" = MDX component markup for React UI
PROMPT_FORMAT=format

# ── Auth (HTTP API only) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JWT algorithm: HS256 or RS256
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
# JWT claim used as user_id for session storage
JWT_USER_ID_CLAIM=sub
# The actual secret — keep this private
JWT_SECRET=your-secret-here
```

> **Note:** `JWT_SECRET` is read by your JWT middleware at verify time. The pipeline
> reads `JWT_ALGORITHM` and `JWT_USER_ID_CLAIM` from config. You need to wire
> your own JWT verification using `JWT_SECRET` if you want full token signature checking
> (the current [extractUserId](file:///Users/amritanshu/Desktop/AI%20Chat%20bot/troubleshooting-poc/server/api/server.ts#29-53) decodes the payload for the claim but does not verify
> the signature — add `jose` or `jsonwebtoken` for production).

---

## 2. What to Add to [package.json](file:///Users/amritanshu/Desktop/AI%20Chat%20bot/troubleshooting-poc/package.json) Scripts

The existing scripts already cover `chat` and `server`. Add these for convenience:

```json
"scripts": {
  "chat": "bun server/cli/chat.ts",
  "server": "bun run server/api/server.ts",

  "chat:user": "bun server/cli/chat.ts --user-id",
  "chat:resume": "bun server/cli/chat.ts --user-id $USER_ID --session-id $SESSION_ID",
  "chat:list": "bun server/cli/chat.ts --user-id $USER_ID --list",
  "chat:show": "bun server/cli/chat.ts --user-id $USER_ID --show $SESSION_ID"
}
```

---

## 3. How to Run

### CLI (dev/test — no auth required)

```bash
# New session as default user (cli-user)
bun run chat

# New session as a specific user
bun server/cli/chat.ts --user-id alice

# Resume an existing session
bun server/cli/chat.ts --user-id alice --session-id <uuid>

# List all sessions for a user
bun server/cli/chat.ts --user-id alice --list

# Print full conversation history for a session
bun server/cli/chat.ts --user-id alice --show <uuid>
```

### HTTP Server

```bash
bun run server
```

Server starts on **http://localhost:3000**

---

## 4. HTTP API Endpoints

### `POST /answer`
Submit a user message and receive an answer.

**Headers:**
```
Authorization: Bearer <jwt>
Content-Type: application/json
```

**Request body:**
```json
{
  "message": "How do I submit a credentialing document?",
  "session_id": "uuid-optional"
}
```
Omit `session_id` to start a new session. Include it to resume.

**Response `200`:**
```json
{
  "session_id": "uuid",
  "action": "respond",
  "response": "formatted markdown response",
  "response_type": "answer",
  "citations": [
    { "chunk_id": "uuid", "source": "procedure.pdf" }
  ]
}
```

**`response_type` values:**

| Value | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `answer` | Direct single-path answer |
| `options` | Multiple paths — user must choose |
| `mixed` | Narrative + conditional branches |
| `clarify` | Question too vague — bot asks for clarification |
| `notfound` | No match found — fallback served |
| `quota_exceeded` | Session turn limit reached → HTTP 429 |

---

### `GET /sessions`
List all sessions for the authenticated user.

**Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`

**Response `200`:**
```json
[
  {
    "session_id": "uuid",
    "title": "How to submit credentialing docs",
    "filename": "20260303_083313_uuid.jsonl",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:45:00Z",
    "turn_count": 4
  }
]
```

---

### `GET /sessions/:sessionId`
Get full turn history for a session.

**Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`

**Response `200`:**
```json
{
  "session_id": "uuid",
  "user_id": "alice",
  "title": "How to submit credentialing docs",
  "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:33:13Z",
  "turns": [
    { "type": "turn", "role": "user", "window": 0, "content": "...", "ts": "..." },
    { "type": "turn", "role": "assistant", "window": 0, "content": "...",
      "citations": [{ "chunk_id": "...", "source": "procedure.pdf" }],
      "duration_ms": 1840, "ts": "..." }
  ]
}
```

**Response `404`:** Session not found

---

### `GET /health`
No auth required.

```json
{ "status": "ok", "breaker": "CLOSED" }
```

---

## 5. HTTP Status Codes

| Code | When |
|------|------|
| `200` | Success |
| `400` | Missing `message` field or bad JSON |
| `401` | Missing/malformed/expired JWT |
| `404` | Session not found |
| `413` | Request body too large (> 64 KB) |
| `429` | Session turn quota exceeded |
| `500` | Pipeline error |
| `503` | Server shutting down |
| `504` | LLM response timed out (120s default) |

---

## 6. Prerequisites

Before the retrieval pipeline can answer anything, the **generation pipeline must have run**:

```bash
# Process a PDF and build the knowledge base
bun run gen:run

# Compile guide.yaml from all processed chunks
bun run gen:compile
```

This produces:
```
generation/output/final/
├── guide.yaml          ← triage index
├── default.md          ← fallback response
└── <uuid>.md           ← individual chunk files
```

The retrieval pipeline reads from this directory. It never writes to it.

---

## 7. Swapping to MDX Format (React UI)

Set in [.env](file:///Users/amritanshu/Desktop/AI%20Chat%20bot/troubleshooting-poc/.env):
```env
PROMPT_FORMAT=format-mdx
```

The formatter will now emit `<Steps>`, `<Callout>`, `<Tabs>` MDX components instead of plain markdown. No code changes needed.
